          "filename": "A boggy plateau - geograph.org.uk - 766885.jpg",
          "caption": "A boggy plateau Much of the \"drainage\" of the Lealt Burn is a waterlogged plain at just over 100m above sea level. This is a difficult area for navigation - pick the wrong ATV track, and these become hard to find when the grass is growing, and you may end up in the wrong west coast glen. Heading eastwards is easy though, eventually you will hit The Road.",
